App Overview
This Android application demonstrates practical implementation of GitHub Actions for automated testing and continuous integration. The app serves as a learning tool for mobile development students to understand CI/CD workflows.

Purpose
The primary goal is to create a functional Android app that integrates with GitHub's automation tools, allowing developers to:

Understand automated build processes
Implement unit testing frameworks
Practice version control with GitHub
GitHub Actions Integration
GitHub Actions automates the build and test pipeline. When code is pushed to the repository, Actions automatically:

Compiles the Android project
Runs all unit tests
Validates code quality
This ensures consistent builds and catches errors early in development.
